{
  \"contract\": \"board-build-plan/v1\",
  \"artifacts\": [
    {
      \"alias\": \"title\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_text\",
        \"text\": \"THE NEXT "'$2M'"\\nOcean Cleanup Portfolio Brief • Board decision draft\",
        \"placement\": {\"target\": {\"kind\": \"auto\"}}
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"recommendation\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"RECOMMENDATION • BALANCED PORTFOLIO\",
        \"body\": \""'$900K — River leakage prevention (45%)'"\\n"'$650K — Ghost gear recovery (32.5%)'"\\n"'$450K — Coastal waste systems (22.5%)'"\\n\\nWhy this mix: lead with scalable prevention, retain a high-ecological-value removal lane, and fund the local systems that make gains durable. Release in gated tranches, not one check.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"portfolio\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"PORTFOLIO • COST + IMPACT\",
        \"body\": \"24-month planning impact: 2,150–3,750 metric tons\\nModeled portfolio cost: "'$533–$930 per ton'"\\nRisk balance: 45% medium / 32.5% medium-high / 22.5% low-medium\\n\\nThese are decision ranges, not audited forecasts. Compare bids on one measurement protocol before committing tranche 2.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"decision\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"BOARD DECISION • APPROVE WITH GATES\",
        \"body\": \"Approve the allocation envelope and measurement rules today. Delegate vendor selection after a 30-day diligence sprint.\\n\\nAuthorize "'$1.2M initial commitments. Hold $800K for milestone release or reallocation at day 90.'"\\n\\nDecision posture: fund operating models, not brand names.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"river\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"A • RIVER LEAKAGE PREVENTION\",
        \"body\": \"ALLOCATE  "'$900K • 45%'"\\nIMPACT  1,200–2,000 t prevented / 24 mo\\nUNIT COST  "'$450–$750 / t'"\\nEXECUTION RISK  MEDIUM\\n\\nDeploy capture + maintenance in two high-load watersheds. Strongest scalable prevention case.\\n\\nWatch: permits, flood-season uptime, local operator capacity, verified disposal chain.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"gear\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"B • GHOST GEAR RECOVERY\",
        \"body\": \"ALLOCATE  "'$650K • 32.5%'"\\nIMPACT  250–450 t removed / 24 mo\\nUNIT COST  "'$1,444–$2,600 / t'"\\nEXECUTION RISK  MEDIUM-HIGH\\n\\nMap, retrieve, and recycle abandoned fishing gear with port and fisher partners. Highest habitat and bycatch co-benefit.\\n\\nWatch: weather, detection yield, vessel access, perverse buyback incentives.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"coastal\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"C • COASTAL WASTE SYSTEMS\",
        \"body\": \"ALLOCATE  "'$450K • 22.5%'"\\nIMPACT  700–1,300 t captured / 24 mo\\nUNIT COST  "'$346–$643 / t'"\\nEXECUTION RISK  LOW-MEDIUM\\n\\nUpgrade collection, sorting, and leakage controls with four coastal municipalities. Best durability and community ownership.\\n\\nWatch: procurement pace, operator retention, contamination, weight-data quality.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"rules\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"DECISION RULES • NON-NEGOTIABLE\",
        \"body\": \"1  FUND only with a baseline, monthly weighed tonnage, geotagged evidence, and named end destination.\\n\\n2  RELEASE tranche 2 only at ≥80% uptime and cost/ton within 125% of plan.\\n\\n3  PAUSE after two missed months or any chain-of-custody failure.\\n\\n4  REALLOCATE uncommitted funds at day 90 to the best verified impact per dollar, while keeping ≥20% in durable local systems.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"weekone\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"FIRST 7 DAYS • THREE ACTIONS\",
        \"body\": \"1  Name one portfolio owner; lock the shared baseline, cost, uptime, safety, and chain-of-custody scorecard.\\n\\n2  Send a 72-hour evidence request to 2–3 operators per program: sites, permits, unit economics, last 12 months of results, references.\\n\\n3  Schedule a day-7 selection huddle; shortlist one lead + one fallback per lane and assign every diligence gap.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"debate\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"BOARD DEBATE • MAKE THE TRADEOFFS EXPLICIT\",
        \"body\": \"• Prevention scale vs. visible removal?\\n• Tons removed vs. habitat value?\\n• Lowest unit cost vs. durable local capacity?\\n• How much of the "'$800K holdback can management reallocate without another vote?'"\\n\\nRecommended answer: optimize verified ocean leakage avoided, not media-friendly cleanup volume.\"
      }
    }
  ],
  \"connections\": [],
  \"layout\": {
    \"kind\": \"grid\",
    \"anchor\": {\"alias\": \"title\"},
    \"members\": [\"recommendation\", \"portfolio\", \"decision\", \"river\", \"gear\", \"coastal\", \"rules\", \"weekone\", \"debate\"],
    \"columns\": 3,
    \"column_gap\": 56,
    \"row_gap\": 56,
    \"align\": \"start\",
    \"placement\": {\"clearance\": 72, \"preferred_directions\": [\"below\"]}
  }
}
